# sentence_id = 60
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = And Zacharias his father was filled with the Holy Spirit and prophesied, saying: "Blessed be the Lord, the God of Israel, because he has visited and redeemed his people, and has raised up a horn of salvation for us in the house of David his servant, just as he spoke through the mouth of his holy prophets from of old, salvation from our enemies and from the hand of all who hate us, to show mercy to our fathers and to remember his holy covenant, the oath which he swore to Abraham our father, to grant us that, delivered from the hand of our enemies, we might serve him without fear, in holiness and righteousness before him all our days."
# literal_translation = And Zacharias the father of him was filled of Spirit holy, and prophesied, saying: Blessed [be the] Lord, the God of Israel, because he visited and made redemption for the people of him, and raised up a horn of salvation for us in [the] house of David the servant of him, just as he spoke through [the] mouth of his holy prophets from of age, salvation out of enemies of us and out of [the] hand of all the ones hating us, to do mercy with the fathers of us and to remember [the] covenant holy of him, [the] oath which he swore to Abraham the father of us, of the [purpose] to give to us, fearlessly, out of [the] hand of enemies having been delivered, to serve him in holiness and righteousness before him in all the days of us.
